.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt SETTINGSHELPER 8
.Os NextBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm SettingsHelper
.Nd make root-only settings changes for the settings apps
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /usr/libexec/SettingsHelper
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes the settings changes that need root, such as the Energy Saver
settings, the time zone, the date and time, network time, the accounts
and the login window's settings, for
NextBSD's settings apps.
It is started by
.Xr launchd 8
on demand as
.Ql org.nextbsd.SettingsHelper ,
serves the Mach service of that name, and exits once it has been idle for
30 seconds and holds no unexpired credential.
It is not meant to be run by hand.
.Pp
Each operation is a typed Mach call (no shell commands and no file paths)
and needs a right named
.Ql org.nextbsd.settings. Ns Ar area .
.Nm
answers only root and processes in the console user's session, as
.Xr loginwindow 8
records it in
.Pa /var/run/loginwindow .
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width "SetLoginWindowOptions"
.It Cm SetPMPreferences
one power source's Energy Saver settings
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.energy .
.It Cm SetTimeZone
copies a zone from
.Pa /usr/share/zoneinfo
to
.Pa /etc/localtime ,
records its name in
.Pa /var/db/zoneinfo ,
as
.Xr tzsetup 8
does, and posts
.Ql com.apple.system.timezone
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.datetime .
.It Cm SetDate
sets the clock with
.Xr settimeofday 2
and posts
.Ql com.apple.system.clock_set
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.datetime .
.It Cm SetNetworkTime
turns
.Ql org.nextbsd.ntpd
on or off with
.Ql launchctl load -w
or
.Ql unload -w ,
and can replace the server and pool lines of
.Pa /etc/ntp.conf
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.datetime .
.It Cm CreateUser
adds an account to the local directory, as
.Xr adduser 8
does: the next free uid, a private group, a password or none, and
optionally group
.Ql admin ;
then builds its home with
.Xr createhomedir 8
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users .
.It Cm DeleteUser
removes an account as
.Xr rmuser 8
does, keeping its home if asked; never the console user or the last
administrator
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users .
.It Cm SetPassword
sets an account's password, or removes it
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users ,
or the console user's own
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users.own-password .
.It Cm SetAdmin
adds an account to group
.Ql admin
or takes it out, never the last one
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users .
.It Cm SetAutoLogin
names the account, one without a password, logged in at startup, or
turns automatic login off
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users .
.It Cm SetLoginWindowOptions
whether the login window asks for a name and password or lists the
users, and whether it shows Restart and Shut Down
.Pq right Ql org.nextbsd.settings.users .
.El
.Pp
The account operations refuse on a machine joined to a directory server,
whose accounts are the server's.
The login settings are Darwin's
.Ql com.apple.loginwindow
keys:
.Ql autoLoginUser
(absent: the only account,
.Ql admin ,
if it has no password; empty: off),
.Ql SHOWFULLNAME ,
.Ql RestartDisabled
and
.Ql ShutDownDisabled .
They apply at the next login window.
.Ss Rights
The rules have the shape of Darwin's authorization database.
Each right names a rule, or is one:
.Bl -tag -width "authenticate-session-owner"
.It Cm allow
anyone in the console session
.It Cm is-admin
the console user is in group
.Ql admin
.It Cm authenticate-admin
an administrator's name and password
.It Cm authenticate-session-owner
the console user's own password
.El
.Pp
A rule's
.Cm timeout
(default 300 seconds) says how long a successful authentication lasts for
the session; 0 makes it good for one change.
Passwords are checked with the PAM service
.Ql authorization
and are never stored.
An administrator whose account has no password authenticates with an
empty one, which the settings apps present as
.Dq Allow changes?
without a password field.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/Local/Library/Security/SettingsRights.plist" -compact
.It Pa /System/Library/Security/SettingsRights.plist
the rights and rules
.It Pa /Local/Library/Security/SettingsRights.plist
a site's rights and rules, which win over the system's
.It Pa /etc/pam.d/authorization
the PAM service passwords are checked with
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.SettingsHelper.plist
the launchd job
.It Pa /etc/localtime , /var/db/zoneinfo
the time zone, as SetTimeZone writes it
.It Pa /etc/ntp.conf
the time server, as SetNetworkTime writes it
.It Pa /Local/Library/DirectoryServices
the local accounts, as the account operations write them
.It Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/org.nextbsd.loginwindow.plist
the login settings, as SetAutoLogin and SetLoginWindowOptions write them
.It Pa /var/log/SettingsHelper.log
its log: who was allowed what, and refusals
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pmset 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr settimeofday 2 ,
.Xr adduser 8 ,
.Xr createhomedir 8 ,
.Xr launchd 8 ,
.Xr ntpd 8 ,
.Xr pam 8 ,
.Xr rmuser 8 ,
.Xr tzsetup 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NextBSD 27.0.
